  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Feed the Future Nigeria Agribusiness Investment Activity</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Nigeria):  The Feed the Future Agribusiness Investment Activity continues to increase the agricultural competitiveness of Nigeria&apos;s smallholder farmers by addressing constraints within the business environment in Nigeria and increasing agriculture-related investment. The activity comprises three main components: 1) increasing the ease of doing business; 2) increasing access to finance; and 3) spurring investment promotion. Overall, the activity improves the agribusiness investment climate, which plays a pivotal role in attracting foreign direct and domestic investments. It also prioritizes partnerships with private sector actors in targeted states.  Nutrition-related businesses, such as those involved in the manufacture of nutrient-rich foods, continue to benefit under this activity. The activity contributes to the Mission&apos;s Feed the Future strategy, which seeks to improve the competitiveness of smallholder farmers and the Administration&apos;s priority of helping Nigerian farmers become self-reliant. These outcomes will be achieved through training, technical assistance, establishing strong working relationships with relevant entities in the public and private sector, and leveraging relationships with investment firms (private equity, venture capital and impact investors) and lead agribusinesses..Through training and clinics, the activity works with local and international business development specialists to build capacity and provide support to women entrepreneurs and women&apos;s associations, including the Women Farmers Advancement Network and the Nigerian Women Agro-Allied Farmers Association.......</narrative>
  </description>
